From: OpenBMC Maintainers <openbmc@lists.ozlabs.org>
Subject: [PATCH] aspeed/ast2600: Enable eSPI and PECI interfaces for Intel platform
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0000

Enable eSPI (Enhanced Serial Peripheral Interface) and PECI (Platform
Environment Control Interface) support in the AST2600 device tree to support
Intel platform BMC integration. This allows:

- eSPI communication with Intel PCH for LPC/eSPI tunneling
- PECI communication for CPU temperature and DIMM temperature monitoring
- Access to CPU and memory thermal information via hwmon

Signed-off-by: OpenBMC Developers <openbmc@lists.ozlabs.org>
---

Note: This is a template patch. Actual device tree modifications depend on:
1. Specific Intel platform (e.g., Eagle Stream, Whitley, Birch Stream)
2. AST2600 pin assignments for eSPI/PECI
3. PECI target device addresses on the bus

The following should be added to aspeed-ast2600-evb.dts or a platform-specific override:

&espi {
    status = "okay";
};

&peci {
    status = "okay";
    // PECI target device configuration for Intel CPUs
    // Example: CPU at 0x30, DIMM temp at 0x31
};

To apply this patch to a real build:
1. Customize the device tree nodes based on your Intel platform
2. Place the actual .dts changes in a proper patch file
3. Ensure proper pin muxing configuration in U-Boot as well
